WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Since ancient times, a group of deer lived in the forest on the banks of the Mississippi River.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:16.000
They considered themselves part of this beautiful nature, until one day, one of them made a huge discovery.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:23.000
It was an innovative way to cook ostrich eggs, a turning point in the history of deer.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:32.000
This clever invention was followed by others like potato peelers and cooking Basmati rice.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:42.000
From that moment, the deer started to hold their heads high, boasting about their power over nature.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:01:00.000
They said, "Who is stronger than us?" Their necks evolved, turning them into giraffes.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:20.000
As they turned into giraffes, their technical progress led them to believe they owned the entire forest.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:02:08.000
They saw themselves as the center of the universe, believing they deserved absolute reward for their deeds.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:30.000
The place became "The Giraffes' Manor," where they decide who enters and who leaves based on their arrogance.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:03:00.000
The current debate is strange; only the owner of the "manor" should set the rules.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:38.000
In the end, a tiny microbe or a common cold reminds them of their true size. Peace be upon you.